scbinder
========

scbinder is a port of Earthworm's phase associator binder_ew to SeisComP.
It is made of two parts with different licenses.


1. Earthworm core — MIT
-----------------------

The following files are carried over verbatim from Earthworm
(https://gitlab.com/seismic-software/earthworm) and remain under
Earthworm's own MIT license (Copyright (c) 2022 Seismic Software):

    core/*.c core/*.h        grid.c, bind.c, hyp.c, l1.c, ingelada.c,
                             linear.c, sample.c, assess.c and headers —
                             originally src/seismic_processing/binder_ew/,
                             the association/nucleation/location algorithm
                             written by Carl Johnson with contributions
                             from the Earthworm community (L. Dietz,
                             P. Friberg and others; see the revision
                             histories preserved in the sources).

    ewlib/*.c ewlib/*.h      kom.c, tlay.c, site.c, geo_to_km.c, brent.c,
                             mnbrak.c, chron3.c, time_ew.c and headers —
                             originally src/libsrc/util/ and include/.

The full MIT license text that must accompany these files is in
LICENSE.earthworm.


2. SeisComP port — GNU AGPL-3.0-or-later
----------------------------------------

All other files (the SeisComP Client::Application adapter under app/, the
regression harness under harness/, the national-grid generator under
tools/, build files, configuration and documentation) are original work:

